; A homogeneous array whose ELEMENT is a plain group WRAPPED in an anonymous array
; (`[* [coords]]`), beside the same array over the BARE plain group (`[* coords]`) as its control.
; The two look one bracket apart and are opposite wire shapes, which is the whole reason both are
; spelled here:
;   `[* coords]`   — the group SPLICES. Each element contributes `coords`'s own field count to the
;                    outer array's length (`2 * n`), and is read through `deserialize_as_embedded_group`.
;   `[* [coords]]` — the wrapper promotes the group to a standalone struct that writes its OWN array
;                    header. Each element is exactly ONE outer item (`1 * n`) and is read through
;                    the standalone `deserialize`.
;
; Both sides of the wire have to agree on which of those two an element is, and the READ-LENGTH
; accounting was the half that did not: the element-read face and the serialize length both consult
; `RustType::is_basic` (plain-group AND not promoted), while the deserialize loop's branch asked only
; `is_plain_group`. So the wrapped element was read standalone — correctly, one outer item — while
; the outer array's budget was charged the group's 2 fields, and the crate emitted bytes its own
; decoder rejected with `DefiniteLenMismatch`. Exit 0, compiles, round-trip red.
;
; Profile-independent: the defect and its fix are the same site under `--preserve-encodings`, which
; reads the length through `array_sz()` but keeps the same per-element accounting.
;
; The MAP positions are deliberately spelled too, as controls that were already green and must stay
; so: a table's length counts ENTRIES, not items, so a wrapped group in either the key or the value
; role costs one slot no matter what it expands to — the array arm is the only one where an
; element's expansion can be charged to its container.
coords = (uint, uint)
spliced_group_array = [inner: [* coords]]
wrapped_group_array = [inner: [* [coords]]]
wrapped_group_map_value = [inner: { * uint => [coords] }]
wrapped_group_map_key = [inner: { * [coords] => uint }]
